{"seq":5,"slug":"theodore-roosevelt-conservation","title":"西奥多·罗斯福：自然保护遗产","stage":"DONE","category":"theodore-roosevelt","categoryLabel":"西奥多·罗斯福","chapterCount":3,"docCount":7,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation","rating":{"composite":3.5,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":2.5,"positioning":null,"strategic":5},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/leaders/10_theodore-roosevelt/5_theodore-roosevelt-conservation","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"西奥多-罗斯福-自然保护遗产\">西奥多·罗斯福：自然保护遗产</h1><p>在西奥多·罗斯福（Theodore Roosevelt，1858—1919）执掌白宫的近八年间（1901—1909），美国联邦政府第一次把&quot;保护自然资源&quot;提升为一项系统性的国家政策。在他离任时，约 2.3 亿英亩（约 93 万平方公里）的公共土地被纳入某种形式的联邦保护之下——这一面积超过当时美国本土的十分之一，至今仍是单一总统任内最庞大的自然保护遗产。</p>\n<p>这份遗产并非凭空而来。罗斯福本人是博物学爱好者、猎人和西部牧场主，他对自然的兴趣可以追溯到童年时期对鸟类的痴迷，并在达科他荒地（Dakota Badlands）的牧场生活中淬炼成一种对消失中的边疆的紧迫感。1887 年，他与一群志同道合的猎人创立布恩与克罗克特俱乐部（Boone and Crockett Club），把&quot;狩猎伦理&quot;转化为最早的有组织保护行动。这些经历构成了他日后政策的思想根基。</p>\n<p>入主白宫后，罗斯福把私人的自然情怀转化为制度建设。他重用吉福德·平肖（Gifford Pinchot），在 1905 年促成林务局（U.S. Forest Service）的成立，把&quot;科学管理、永续利用&quot;的功利主义保护理念植入联邦行政体系；他借助 1906 年《古物法》（Antiquities Act）的总统授权，绕开国会单方面设立国家纪念地；他以行政命令发明了国家野生动物保护区系统，从 1903 年的佩利肯岛（Pelican Island）起步。</p>\n<p>然而，罗斯福的保护事业从一开始就交织着深刻的张力与争议。功利主义的&quot;保育&quot;（conservation）与约翰·缪尔（John Muir）所代表的&quot;保存&quot;（preservation）理念在赫奇赫奇（Hetch Hetchy）峡谷的存废之争中正面冲突；更尖锐的是，被宣告为&quot;荒野&quot;的土地，许多本是原住民世代生活与管理的家园，保护区的设立往往伴随对印第安人的驱逐与边缘化。</p>\n<p>本 hub 试图以严谨、平衡、有据可查的方式呈现这份复杂遗产：它既追溯理念的源头，也细究总统任期内的具体制度与立法，更直面其内在矛盾与当代（2020 年代）史学界对其的重新评估。读者将看到一个既是先驱、又非完人的历史人物，以及一套至今仍在塑造美国土地与环境政治的制度框架。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"roots-of-a-conservation-ethic","title":"自然保护理念的根源","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/roots-of-a-conservation-ethic","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"naturalist-and-hunter","title":"博物学家与猎人：罗斯福的自然养成","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/roots-of-a-conservation-ethic/naturalist-and-hunter"},{"seq":2,"slug":"boone-and-crockett-and-intellectual-foundations","title":"布恩与克罗克特俱乐部与思想基础","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/roots-of-a-conservation-ethic/boone-and-crockett-and-intellectual-foundations"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-conservation-presidency","title":"自然保护总统任期","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/the-conservation-presidency","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"forest-service-and-pinchot","title":"林务局与平肖：功利保育的制度化","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/the-conservation-presidency/forest-service-and-pinchot"},{"seq":2,"slug":"antiquities-act-and-national-monuments","title":"《古物法》与国家纪念地：行政权的扩张","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/the-conservation-presidency/antiquities-act-and-national-monuments"},{"seq":3,"slug":"wildlife-refuges-and-national-parks","title":"野生动物保护区与国家公园","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/the-conservation-presidency/wildlife-refuges-and-national-parks"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"controversies-and-legacy","title":"争议与遗产","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/controversies-and-legacy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"preservation-versus-utilitarian-conservation","title":"保存与保育之争：赫奇赫奇的分水岭","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/controversies-and-legacy/preservation-versus-utilitarian-conservation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"reassessing-the-legacy","title":"重估遗产：原住民、种族与当代视角","url":"/l-doc-books/c/leaders/theodore-roosevelt/theodore-roosevelt-conservation/controversies-and-legacy/reassessing-the-legacy"}]}]}